# `= =` with a space: one DS0110 with a fix to `==`.
mode: syntax
---- query
t | where a = = 1
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..18
  PIPELINE@0..17
    NAME_REF@0..1
      IDENT@0..1 "t"
    WHITESPACE@1..2 " "
    PIPE@2..3 "|"
    WHITESPACE@3..4 " "
    WHERE_OP@4..17
      IDENT@4..9 "where"
      WHITESPACE@9..10 " "
      BIN_EXPR@10..17
        NAME_REF@10..11
          IDENT@10..11 "a"
        WHITESPACE@11..12 " "
        EQ@12..13 "="
        WHITESPACE@13..14 " "
        EQ@14..15 "="
        WHITESPACE@15..16 " "
        LITERAL@16..17
          LONG@16..17 "1"
  WHITESPACE@17..18 "\n"

error[DS0110]: `= =` is not an operator
  --> query:1:13
  |
1 | t | where a = = 1
  |             ^^^
  |
  = help: use `==` to compare values: `a == 1`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    t | where a == 1
which parses without errors
